# gent-talk launcher configuration — EXAMPLE. Copy it, then fill it in:
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/gent-talk
#   cp gent-talk/gent-talk.env.example ~/.config/gent-talk/env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/gent-talk/env
#   gent-talk/scripts/run.sh
#
# This file is sourced by a shell (gent-talk/scripts/run.sh), so it is shell syntax: NAME=value,
# no spaces around `=`, and quote anything containing a space, a comma or a colon.
#
# WHERE IT IS READ FROM, in increasing precedence:
#   1. ~/.config/gent-talk/env      — the one and only default location, shared by every checkout
#                                     on this machine.
#   2. Variables already exported in your shell — these beat the file.
# Passing `--config FILE` to run.sh replaces the file layer: that file, and nothing else.
#
# There is deliberately no second, in-checkout config location. One file that is always the live
# one beats two files and a rule about which wins.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy. Keeping the real file under ~/.config puts it outside every git
# checkout; if you keep yours somewhere else, make sure that path is ignored.
#
# This is the LAUNCHER's environment-variable configuration. It is a different thing from
# gent-talk.example.toml, which is the SERVER's own config-file format for the same settings —
# the server reads either, and the environment wins. Use this file with scripts/run.sh; use the
# TOML when you would rather mount a config file into the container.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. run.sh refuses to build or launch unless all four are set to non-placeholder values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bot token for the SECOND, dedicated Discord bot — not the one your coding agents use.
GENT_TALK_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME

# The credentials THIS server demands of its own callers (not Discord's, not ElevenLabs').
# Generate each with:  openssl rand -base64 33
# The read token goes in your phone and in the voice agent's tool configuration. The write token
# lets something post as your bot — hand it out far more carefully.
GENT_TALK_READ_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME-at-least-24-characters
GENT_TALK_WRITE_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME-different-and-at-least-24-characters

# The channel ALLOWLIST: comma-separated `<channel-id>:<label>:rw` entries (`:ro` for read-only).
# A channel that is not listed cannot be read or posted to even with a valid token. `ro` is the
# safe choice; only use `rw` where you want the bridge to be able to speak.
# run.sh checks the shape of every entry, because a typo here otherwise surfaces only at startup.
GENT_TALK_CHANNELS="123456789012345678:lead team:rw,987654321098765432:build noise:ro"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — server. Unset means the feature is off; nothing here blocks a launch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Voice (/voice and GET /api/v1/signed-url) needs BOTH of these. With either one missing, the
# signed-url endpoint answers 503 and names what is missing; it never falls back to an unsigned
# URL. agent_id is public; the API key is an account secret that can spend money.
#GENT_TALK_ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=agent_...
#GENT_TALK_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=REPLACE-ME

# Only set this to reach a regional endpoint, a proxy, or the offline vendor substitute
# (`cargo run --bin gent-talk-mock-elevenlabs`), which mints a real signed URL onto a real local
# WebSocket for free. That is the second legitimate use, and the only one you will want locally.
#GENT_TALK_ELEVENLABS_API_BASE=https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1
#GENT_TALK_ELEVENLABS_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18092/v1

# The URL this server is reachable at from outside. Recorded so the deployment is self-describing.
#GENT_TALK_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://gent-talk.example.net

# YOUR time zone, as an IANA name. Every message time is converted into it once, on the server,
# and handed onward already labelled ("09:51:25 EDT") so the voice agent reads it out without
# converting anything. Defaults to UTC. An unknown name stops the server rather than silently
# becoming UTC — the whole point is that a confidently-spoken time is in the right zone. The
# database is compiled into the binary, so the container needs no tzdata package.
#GENT_TALK_TIMEZONE=America/New_York

# Set to 1 to start without the per-channel startup probe. The probe reads one message from every
# allowlisted channel and refuses to start if it cannot — it is what catches "the bot is in the
# server but was never added to this private channel". Skipping it is logged loudly.
#GENT_TALK_SKIP_STARTUP_PROBE=1

# Log filter for the server process.
#RUST_LOG=info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — launcher. These configure scripts/run.sh itself, not the server.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Image to build and run, and where to publish it. run.sh detects an already-running instance by
# this image reference OR this host port — never by container name, which podman regenerates on
# every launch.
#GENT_TALK_IMAGE_NAME=gent-talk
#GENT_TALK_IMAGE_TAG=v0
#GENT_TALK_HOST_PORT=8080
# 127.0.0.1 keeps the port off the LAN; the tunnel (below) is how it reaches the internet.
#GENT_TALK_HOST_ADDR=127.0.0.1

# podman by default; set to docker if that is what you have.
#GENT_TALK_ENGINE=podman

# The cloudflared tunnel check. OFF by default: without it run.sh never looks at systemd.
# Turn it on where the public hostname is served by a `systemctl --user` cloudflared unit — run.sh
# then verifies the unit is active and starts it if it is not, before launching the container.
# Override for a single run with --tunnel / --no-tunnel.
#GENT_TALK_TUNNEL_ENABLED=1
#GENT_TALK_TUNNEL_UNIT=cloudflared-gent-talk.service

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — durable state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path to the SQLite file holding /voice transcripts and read marks. Unset means this
# server keeps nothing between restarts and says so. The image already sets this to a path it
# declares as a VOLUME, so you normally set GENT_TALK_DATA_DIR below instead of this.
#GENT_TALK_STORAGE_PATH=/var/lib/gent-talk/gent-talk.sqlite3

# Launcher setting: the HOST directory bind-mounted at /var/lib/gent-talk. This is the thing that
# actually makes state survive a rebuild — without a mount, the container's copy is destroyed the
# next time run.sh replaces it. run.sh creates it 0700 if it is missing.
#GENT_TALK_DATA_DIR=$HOME/.local/share/gent-talk

# The model a summariser is asked for. Unset means the shipped extractive backend (truncation, no
# model, no network, no cost). Changing this invalidates every cached summary, by design.
#GENT_TALK_SUMMARY_MODEL=
